        "has_text_layer": true,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "title",
            "text": "Column-Aware Text Extraction with Traceable Evidence",
            "bbox": [
              25.2,
              726.0,
              586.8,
              726.0
            ],
            "font_size": 18.0,
            "line_count": 1
          },
          {
            "type": "authors",
            "text": "A. Researcher, B. Reviewer",
            "bbox": [
              212.4,
              704.0,
              399.6,
              704.0
            ],
            "font_size": 12.0,
            "line_count": 1
          },
          {
            "type": "authors",
            "text": "Institute of Document Analysis",
            "bbox": [
              207.0,
              690.0,
              405.0,
              690.0
            ],
            "font_size": 11.0,
            "line_count": 1
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "text": "Abstract",
            "bbox": [
              56.0,
              662.0,
              108.8,
              662.0
            ],
            "font_size": 11.0,
            "line_count": 1
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "We present a layout reader that reconstructs two-column reading order from glyph geometry, keeps a page and bounding box for every character, and reports unreadable regions instead of guessing them.",
            "bbox": [
              44.0,
              624.0,
              492.2,
              646.0
            ],
            "font_size": 9.0,
            "line_count": 3
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "text": "1 Introduction",
            "bbox": [
              56.0,
              560.0,
              155.0,
              560.0
            ],
            "font_size": 11.0,
            "line_count": 1
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Text extraction from research papers is usually evaluated on rendered pages, not on the structure a reader needs. A sentence that begins in the left column and ends in the right column is a sentence no reader ever wrote, yet column interleaving produces exactly that artefact.",
            "bbox": [
              56.0,
              456.0,
              296.0,
              540.0
            ],
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "line_count": 8
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "The failure is easy to miss because the words are all present and the character count looks healthy. Only a reader notices that the grammar has collapsed.",
            "bbox": [
              56.0,
              402.0,
              290.0,
              438.0
            ],
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "line_count": 4
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "We treat reading order as a geometric problem: glyph boxes are cut recursively along whitespace, so a vertical cut yields columns that are emitted left to right before any line inside them is assembled.",
            "bbox": [
              56.0,
              324.0,
              296.0,
              384.0
            ],
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "line_count": 6
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "text": "2 Method",
            "bbox": [
              316.0,
              560.0,
              375.4,
              560.0
            ],
            "font_size": 11.0,
            "line_count": 1
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Two properties matter for downstream use. First, every character keeps a page and a bounding box, so a claim can be traced back to the spot it came from. Second, the extractor reports what it could not read instead of smoothing it over.",
            "bbox": [
              316.0,
              468.0,
              556.0,
              540.0
            ],
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "line_count": 7
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Reproducibility of the layout analysis is what makes the second property useful: a reviewer can rerun the same page and obtain the same boxes.",
            "bbox": [
              316.0,
              414.0,
              544.0,
              450.0
            ],
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "line_count": 4
          }
        ],
        "removed_headers_footers": [
          {
            "text": "Preprint - do not distribute",
            "kind": "header_or_footer",
            "bbox": [
              56.0,
              762.0,
              190.4,
              762.0
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "1",
            "kind": "header_or_footer",
            "bbox": [
              303.3,
              40.0,
              308.7,
              40.0
            ]
          }
        ],
        "images": []
      },
      {
        "page": 2,
        "width": 612.0,
        "height": 792.0,
        "char_count": 1039,
        "has_text_layer": true,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "text": "3 Results",
            "bbox": [
              56.0,
              720.0,
              122.0,
              720.0
            ],
            "font_size": 11.0,
            "line_count": 1
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "The recursive cut is applied to glyph boxes rather than to finished lines. Line assembly needs a column decision first, and a column decision made per line oscillates on justified text where the right edge is ragged.",
            "bbox": [
              56.0,
              640.0,
              290.0,
              700.0
            ],
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "line_count": 6
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Header and footer removal is decided per document, not per page: a band line is dropped only when the same normalised text recurs across pages.",
            "bbox": [
              56.0,
              586.0,
              296.0,
              622.0
            ],
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "line_count": 4
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Tables are detected from aligned whitespace columns. A candidate needs at least three rows, consistent column starts and numeric content before it is reported.",
            "bbox": [
              316.0,
              652.0,
              556.0,
              700.0
            ],
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "line_count": 5
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "When the heuristic declines, the block stays ordinary text and the result says no table was found, which is the honest outcome for a two-column page body.",
            "bbox": [
              316.0,
              598.0,
              550.0,
              634.0
            ],
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "line_count": 4
          },
          {
            "type": "caption",
            "text": "Table 1: Extraction accuracy on the two-column set.",
            "bbox": [
              56.0,
              560.0,
              346.7,
              560.0
            ],
            "font_size": 9.5,
            "line_count": 1
          },
          {
            "type": "table",
            "text": "Model Precision Recall F1 baseline 0.812 0.774 0.793 column-cut 0.965 0.958 0.961 column-cut+anchors 0.971 0.960 0.965",
            "bbox": [
              56.0,
              505.0,
              497.0,
              544.0
            ],
            "font_size": 9.0,
            "line_count": 4
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "text": "4 Conclusion",
            "bbox": [
              56.0,
              430.0,
              141.8,
              430.0
            ],
            "font_size": 11.0,
            "line_count": 1
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Reading order belongs to the page geometry, not to the text string. Cutting glyph boxes first and assembling lines second keeps columns apart and keeps every character traceable.",
            "bbox": [
              44.0,
              388.0,
              566.0,
              412.0
            ],
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "line_count": 3
          }
        ],
        "removed_headers_footers": [
